      "title": "String Quartet: Assistant Teaching Professors",
      "description": "MUSI-230-087 - University of Victoria This website stores cookies on your computer. These cookies are used to collect information about how you interact with our website and allow us to remember your browser. We use this information to improve and customize your browsing experience, for analytics and metrics about our visitors both on this website and other media, and for marketing purposes. By using this website, you accept and agree to be bound by UVic’s Terms of Use for web and social media privacy .  If you do not agree to the above, you can configure your browser’s setting to “do not track.” Close Skip to main content Search Start page Search People Departments Maps Buildings Rooms A-Z University of Victoria Apply Library Search Sign in Online tools Sign out Show menu Faculty & staff Careers Academic leadership opportunities Faculty & librarian postings Staff postings Casual work Why work at UVic? Fair hiring & employment Pay & benefits Benefit handbooks Collective agreements Salaries & payroll Professional development Leaves & vacation Pensions & retirement Recognition & service Financial services & payroll Campus services Food & catering Transportation & parking Booking space Facilities requests Computer help & technology Safety & security Crisis & emergency supports Health & wellness Marketing & communications Hire a co-op student Career support services ONECard Bookstore Academics & research Advising framework Awards & honours Entrepreneurship International agreements Invention management Learning & teaching Library services Organizing field schools Registrar services & systems Research support Strategic initiatives Organization & governance About UVic Organization structure Our leadership Plans & strategies Campus update sessions Indigenous protocols & resources Policies & guidelines Privacy & access to information Info for... Info for... New faculty & staff Managers & supervisors Home Careers Faculty & librarian positions String Quartet: Assistant Teaching Professors String Quartet: Assistant Teaching Professors Requirements Additional information Contact information Application deadline Equity statement Rank: 4 Assistant Teaching Professors (0.5 FTE) tenure-track, in Strings (String Quartet) (Violin I, Violin II, Viola, and Cello) Start Date: July 1, 2027 We acknowledge and respect the Lək̓ʷəŋən (Songhees and Xʷsepsəm/Esquimalt) Peoples on whose territory the university stands, and the Lək̓ʷəŋən and W̱SÁNEĆ Peoples whose historical relationships with the land continue to this day.  We are privileged to do our work in a way that is inspired by their history, customs and culture. Please review the University’s video “ Welcome to the Territory ” for more information. The University of Victoria School of Music invites applications from members of a professional string quartet for four 0.5 FTE tenure-track Assistant Teaching Professor appointments in Strings (Violin I, Violin II, Viola, and Cello). General Information The UVic School of Music is dedicated to experiential learning and training for musicians and music scholars, turning passion into profession. We are proud to be the only “All Steinway School of Music” in Canada. The School is home to 45 performers, composers, educators, theorists, musicologists, and professional staff, as well as 200 undergraduate majors and 40 graduate students. We offer Bachelor of Music degrees in composition, music education, performance, musicology and sound studies, and musical arts along with a combined degree in Music and Computer Science and a Bachelor of Arts in Music. The School offers graduate degrees in composition, performance, musicology and sound studies, and music technology. We are strongly committed to inclusive excellence and equity and to increasing the diversity of approaches and perspectives in teaching, research, and creative output. Salary Range The candidate's qualifications, experience and overall market demand will determine a candidate’s final salary offer. The salary for this 0.5 FTE Assistant Teaching Professor position includes a competitive salary range of $99,000 to $122,000, prorated for a 0.5 FTE. UVic is committed to offering an equitable and competitive salary, inclusive of a generous benefits package, eligible leaves and pension plan. Requirements Applications will be considered only from existing string quartets whose members all wish to be appointed in simultaneous but individual contracts. The successful candidates will each hold a 0.5 FTE Assistant Teaching Professor (“ATP”) appointment and will all be expected to maintain an active professional profile as a string quartet while contributing to the musical and academic life of the School through teaching, mentorship, creative activity, student recruitment, and service. Responsibilities of the successful candidates will include: Teaching applied lessons in their respective string disciplines, coaching chamber music ensembles at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and recruiting students; Contributing to the School's curriculum through teaching in chamber music, string performance, and potentially in additional areas, depending on the needs of the School, such as musicology, music theory, composition, music technology, music education, or a related field; Mentoring students in musical, academic, and professional development; Engaging in teaching-stream scholarly activities, including maintaining an active professional profile as a string quartet through performances, recordings, masterclasses, workshops, and community-engaged activities that enhance the artistic profile of the School, Faculty, and University; Engaging the university and greater Victoria community through concerts ; Participating in service activities including committee work, jury and audition adjudication, and initiatives that advance the strategic priorities of the School, Faculty, and University. Selection Criteria Assessment of applications will consider both the collective achievements of the quartet and the qualifications, experience, and potential of the individual members. Applications will be assessed on the basis of the following criteria: Demonstrated excellence and achievement as a professional string quartet; Evidence of a professional reputation at the national and/or international level, including but not limited to: performances, masterclasses, recordings, commissions, awards, festival invitations, and/or competition participation; Evidence of teaching effectiveness in applied individual string instruction; Demonstrated experience in chamber music coaching and pedagogy; Capacity to contribute to the broader School of Music curriculum through teaching in an additional area, if needed, such as performance practice, musicology, music theory, composition, music technology, music education, or related fields; Capacity to engage in scholarly activity appropriate to a teaching stream appointment as described in UVIC’s Faculty Collective Agreement (e.g. performances, masterclasses, workshops, and community-engaged activities); Commitment to student mentorship and recruitment; Demonstrated ability or potential to contribute positively to a collegial academic environment through service, collaboration, and professional conduct; Commitment to fostering inclusive, equitable, and supportive learning environments. Assets The following qualifications and experiences will be considered assets for individual members of the quartet but are not required: International artistic recognition through: recordings, commissions, awards, festival invitations, competition successes, experience as a member of a quartet-in-residence; Experience teaching graduate students and/or advanced chamber music; ensembles; Demonstrated awareness and promotion of a broad array of composers and repertoires and musical styles; Demonstrated success in student recruitment and program development; Community-engaged educational or outreach initiatives; Interdisciplinary musical or scholarly collaborations; Evidence of leadership within academic, musical, or community settings. The anticipated start date for these appointments is July 1, 2027. Additional information Faculty and Librarians at the University of Victoria are governed by the provisions of the Collective Agreement .  Members are represented by the University of Victoria Faculty Association . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply. If you are neither a Canadian citizen or permanent resident, please indicate if you are authorized to work in Canada or willingness to apply for authorization, if offered a position contingent upon eligibility and approval from Canadian government authorities. Contact information Applications should be received no later than October 1 st , 2026. Applications will be accepted only from existing string quartets whose members are applying collectively for the four appointments. Please submit the following joint materials (submitted on behalf of the quartet) electronically to music@uvic.ca : A cover letter (1-2 pages) describing the quartet's interest in the position and addressing the qualifications, responsibilities, and selection criteria outlined in the advertisement; A resumé (maximum 2 pages) outlining the quartet's creative activity, professional achievements, and proposed contributions to the School of Music; Appropriate evidence of the quartet's artistic and creative activity, such as links to recordings, performances, external reviews or other professional accomplishments; Contact information for three referees who can speak to the quartet's artistic accomplishments and professional activities. In addition, individual application materials should also be submitted to music@uvic.ca by each member of the quartet: A cover letter (1-2 pages) outlining the candidate's teaching experience, scholarly, creative and/or professional activities and future plans. A curriculum vitae 2 confidential reference letters sent directly by the referees to music@uvic.ca Additional materials may be requested from shortlisted candidates. Please note that reference and background checks, including credential and degree verification, may be undertaken as part of this recruitment process. Application deadline Applications should be received no later than October 1 st , 2026. Equity statement UVic is committed to upholding the values of equity, diversity, inclusion and human rights in our living, learning and work environments. In pursuit of our values, we seek members who are eager to actively participate in that shared responsibility. We actively encourage applications from members of historically and systemically marginalized groups . Read our full equity statement . The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of research achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. Persons with disabilities, who anticipate needing accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, may contact Faculty Relations and Academic Administration in the Office of the VP Academic and Provost at FRrecruit@uvic.ca. Any personal information provided will be maintained in confidence. ​ UVic Instagram ​ UVic Facebook ​ UVic Twitter ​ UVic Linkedin ​ UVic YouTube View all UVic social media Quicklinks About UVic Admissions Research News & media Events Careers Donate Info for... Students Faculty & staff Alumni Indigenous International 2SLGBTQIA+ Business & industry Community University of Victoria 3800 Finnerty Road Victoria BC  V8P 5C2 Canada ​ Maps ​ Hours ​ Contacts Terms of use Accessibility Emergency contacts © University of Victoria Website feedback Back to top of page"
    },
    "https://www.uvic.ca/faculty-staff/careers/faculty-and-librarian-postings/current/atwp_250_112.php": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor",
      "description": "ATWP 250-112 - University of Victoria This website stores cookies on your computer. These cookies are used to collect information about how you interact with our website and allow us to remember your browser. We use this information to improve and customize your browsing experience, for analytics and metrics about our visitors both on this website and other media, and for marketing purposes. By using this website, you accept and agree to be bound by UVic’s Terms of Use for web and social media privacy .  If you do not agree to the above, you can configure your browser’s setting to “do not track.” Close Skip to main content Search Start page Search People Departments Maps Buildings Rooms A-Z University of Victoria Apply Library Search Sign in Online tools Sign out Show menu Faculty & staff Careers Academic leadership opportunities Faculty & librarian postings Staff postings Casual work Why work at UVic? Fair hiring & employment Pay & benefits Benefit handbooks Collective agreements Salaries & payroll Professional development Leaves & vacation Pensions & retirement Recognition & service Financial services & payroll Campus services Food & catering Transportation & parking Booking space Facilities requests Computer help & technology Safety & security Crisis & emergency supports Health & wellness Marketing & communications Hire a co-op student Career support services ONECard Bookstore Academics & research Advising framework Awards & honours Entrepreneurship International agreements Invention management Learning & teaching Library services Organizing field schools Registrar services & systems Research support Strategic initiatives Organization & governance About UVic Organization structure Our leadership Plans & strategies Campus update sessions Indigenous protocols & resources Policies & guidelines Privacy & access to information Info for... Info for... New faculty & staff Managers & supervisors Home Careers Faculty & librarian positions Assistant Teaching Professor Assistant Teaching Professor Requirements Additional information Contact information Application deadline Equity statement We acknowledge and respect the Lək̓ʷəŋən (Songhees and Xʷsepsəm/Esquimalt) Peoples on whose territory the University of Victoria stands, and the Lək̓ʷəŋən and W̱SÁNEĆ Peoples whose historical relationships with the land continue to this day. The Academic and Technical Writing Program (ATWP) at the University of Victoria invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor to commence 1 July 2027. The successful candidate will be appointed into the Faculty of Humanities. SALARY RANGE The candidate's qualifications, experience and overall market demand will determine a candidate’s final salary offer. The salary for this position includes a competitive salary range of $100,000 - $124,000. UVic is committed to offering an equitable and competitive salary, inclusive of a generous benefits package, eligible leaves and pension plan. Requirements ESSENTIAL CRITERIA PhD in a relevant field with specializations in one or more major areas of study in Writing Studies and/or Rhetoric and Composition; Experience with and support of teaching that prioritizes student well-being and the success of students (including individuals from historically marginalized and colonized populations); Experience and/or interest in ongoing learning and professional development in the field of Engineering Communication and/or Technical Writing. DESIRABLE CRITERIA A scholarly focus on writing program administration/coordination, programmatic assessment, curricular design, writing pedagogy, or related area; Demonstrated experience teaching technical writing at the undergraduate level; Demonstrated teaching experience with Indigenous students and/or research interest in Indigenous pedagogies; Demonstrated research interest in anti-racist pedagogies; Published research in Writing Studies or a related field; Experience working as a professional or technical writer. Additional information Faculty and Librarians at the University of Victoria are governed by the provisions of the Collective Agreement . Members are represented by the University of Victoria Faculty Association . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply. If you are neither a Canadian citizen or permanent resident, please indicate if you are authorized to work in Canada or willingness to apply for authorization, if offered a position contingent upon eligibility and approval from Canadian government authorities. Contact information APPLICATION PROCESS To be considered, please send: To be considered, please send the following materials: An application letter of no more than two single-spaced pages that addresses the full scope of the job requirements (explaining your interest in the position, relevant experience and skills, and approach to writing pedagogy; indicates clearly your current legal status to work in Canada as one of the following: Canadian citizen, Canadian permanent resident, Canadian work permit holder, or person eligible to become a Canadian permanent resident. An up-to-date CV. The names of three references who are willing to provide letters of support for this application. A curated and organized teaching dossier totalling no more than 25 pages comprised of A 1- to 2-page statement on your philosophy for teaching writing that includes discussion of efforts to support diversity and accessibility in the classroom; A selection of documents that exemplify claims made in the teaching philosophy statement and offer evidence of helping students grow as writers in academic and/or technical writing classes. These documents may take the form of course outlines, assignment prompts, and/or other teaching materials as well as course evaluation data, teaching observations, and/or student testimonials. Send application materials as email attachments (in Word or PDF electronic format) to atwpadmin@uvic.ca ; please put “ATWP Hiring Committee” in the subject line of your message. To be considered, application packages must be received by midnight (PDT) on September 10, 2026. For more information, please contact Dr. Erin E. Kelly or Dr. Steven Accardi, co-chairs of the Appointment Committee, by writing to atwpdir@uvic.ca . Please note that reference checks will be done, and background checks, including credential and degree verification, may be undertaken as part of this recruitment process. Application deadline Midnight (PDT) on September 10, 2026 Equity statement UVic is committed to upholding the values of equity, diversity, inclusion and human rights in our living, learning and work environments. In pursuit of our values, we seek members who are eager to actively participate in that shared responsibility. We actively encourage applications from members of historically and systemically marginalized groups Read our full equity statement . The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of research achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process may contact Faculty Relations and Academic Administration in the Office of the VP Academic and Provost at FRrecruit@uvic.ca . Any personal information provided will be maintained in confidence. ​ UVic Instagram ​ UVic Facebook ​ UVic Twitter ​ UVic Linkedin ​ UVic YouTube View all UVic social media Quicklinks About UVic Admissions Research News & media Events Careers Donate Info for... Students Faculty & staff Alumni Indigenous International 2SLGBTQIA+ Business & industry Community University of Victoria 3800 Finnerty Road Victoria BC  V8P 5C2 Canada ​ Maps ​ Hours ​ Contacts Terms of use Accessibility Emergency contacts © University of Victoria Website feedback Back to top of page"
    },
